Package: pulzr-usb-gadget
Provides: parkeze-usb-gadget
Replaces: parkeze-usb-gadget
Conflicts: parkeze-usb-gadget
Depends: pulzr-tui, umdns, dnsmasq-full
Maintainer: Joseph Telaak <joseph@pulzr.net>
Architecture: all
Description: The console over a USB cable, as a network and a serial port.
 Presents the board's USB device port to a laptop as a network interface —
 with an address from DHCP and the gateway at pulzr.local — and as a serial
 port running the terminal UI. For boards whose SoC has a USB device
 controller wired to a connector; see PACKAGES_USB_GADGET in
 boards/common/board.conf.
 .
 The kernel modules are not dependencies: they are per target, and only the
 targets with a device controller have them. PACKAGES_USB_GADGET installs
 them alongside this on the boards that take the feature.
